@startuml
title E08 - Security, privacy and tenant isolation
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Primary caregiver" as Caregiver
actor "Unauthorized cross-home actor" as Attacker
participant "OIDC identity provider" as IdP
boundary "A05\nApp platform" as A05
control "B01\nIdentity/access" as B01
control "B02\nHome/consent" as B02
control "B06\nFleet/config" as B06
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
control "S03\nFirmware security/update" as S03
control "T01\nSimulation/CI" as T01
Caregiver -> IdP: Authenticate and obtain audience/issuer-bound token
Caregiver -> A05: Request home data or command
A05 -> B01: Present token, home ID and required permission
B01 -> B02: Resolve active home-scoped membership and consent
B01 -> B06: Authorize device/config action only for same home
B01 -> B08: Audit allowed action without exposing secrets
Attacker -> B01: Attempt cross-home access/rebind
B01 --> Attacker: Reject as unauthorized/not found
S03 -> B06: Require valid credential/update policy for device lifecycle
T01 -> B01: Execute tenant-isolation and fail-closed host tests
note over B02,B08: Resident consent and privacy mode are explicit product states, not implied by purchase or activity.
note over Caregiver,T01: Outcome - Every actor/device action is home-scoped, consent-aware, auditable and fail-closed across security boundaries.
@enduml
